  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ubumbano Voice, Solidarity Support and Accompaniment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project provides a platform for activists and Community Based Organisations in South Africa, Zimbabwe, Zambia, Malawi, Mozambique and Swaziland, to be given financial support, accompaniment and solidarity in telling stories of their struggles. The project compliments CA advocacy and policy work by other regional partners All Africa Conference of Churches, Side-by-Side and Tax Justice Network Africa. There are concrete plans to:
&gt; Consolidate the groups that have already been trained in these countries, 
&gt;&#xA0;Strengthen the moderation and coordination mechanisms, and
&gt; Expand the training to areas where there is interest.
A new initiative called Yetu Collective, will strengthen the project through the following platforms:
&gt; Mamela.org is envisaged as an online home for those organisations and activists without their own websites - a platform where grassroots groups and movements can publish their content online and share it with journalists, as well as offering progressive Civil Society activists a space to promote their views and giving journalists access to a database of content experts.
&gt;&#xA0;Vuka.news is envisaged as a &#x2018;landing page from below&#x2019; - a platform where news, opinion and resources from progressive websites (NGOs, Unions, Alternative media, and Mamaela.org) is aggregated and promoted to an audience that each website cannot reach alone.</narrative>
  </description>
